# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows; the deployment target is Linux. Without this,
# a shell script committed from a Windows checkout carries CRLF, and the kernel
# then reads the shebang as "/usr/bin/env bash\r" — which fails on the server
# with the singularly unhelpful:
#
#     bash: line 1: /tmp/release.sh: cannot execute: required file not found
#
# The scripts under deploy/bin are fetched from S3 and executed on the EC2, so
# they must be LF regardless of who committed them or how their git is
# configured.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.Caddyfile text eol=lf
